    {
      "index": 19,
      "text": "Move To... This element is a more accessible alternative to drag & drop reordering. Press Enter or Space to move this question. Question 3 Not yet graded / 1 pts Edit this Question Delete this Question 0 essay_question <strong data-start=\"1251\" data-end=\"1287\">Reflecting on accountability:</strong><br data-start=\"1287\" data-end=\"1290\">What does <strong data-start=\"1300\" data-end=\"1318\">accountability</strong> look like in a lab group? Give an example of how someone can show accountability, or describe a situation where accountability made a difference. Reflecting on accountability:What does accountability look like in a lab group? Give an example of how someone can show accountability, or describe a situation where accountability made a difference. Your Answer: Accountability in a lab group means following through on the tasks you agree to complete and letting the group know early if something changes. For example, if someone is responsible for entering data or working on part of the report, they should complete it by the agreed time or communicate ahead of time if they need help."
    },
